# AI Agent & Cursor Rules (.cursorrules)

You are working on the `kshatralabs-website` repository ("Engineering the Unmanned Future").
Before performing any task, writing any code, or suggesting modifications, you MUST read and abide by the following core files located in the project root:

1. `prd.md` - Product Requirements Document
2. `architecture.md` (and `architechture.md`) - System Architecture & Technical Stack
3. `rules.md` - Strict Coding & Engineering Rules
4. `phases.md` - Project Roadmap & Implementation Phases
5. `design.md` - Design System & UI Tokens
6. `memory.md` - Project Memory & Context Log

## Key Mandatory Rules:
- Always use strict TypeScript and Next.js 16 App Router conventions.
- Always include `'use client';` at the top of React components using browser hooks, window/document objects, or Three.js/Spline 3D canvases.
- Always use `next/dynamic` with `{ ssr: false }` when importing 3D Spline or WebGL scenes.
- Maintain the tactical, dark-mode glassmorphism aesthetics (`#000000` base, `#cc1414` defense red accents, `Space Grotesk` headings, and `Rajdhani` monospace technical labels).
- Keep `memory.md` and `phases.md` updated as you complete major tasks or make architectural decisions.
